# A spell cast without paying its mana cost still gets its optional additional costs (CR 601.2b, 601.2f, 118.9d), and a cast made
# as an effect resolves is not bound by timing, so the Harbinger's flash permission is never owed there: it is a plain question,
# and here it is answered yes (the rulings allow paying {2} more to cast it without flash trouble). Bot1 casts Bloodbraid
# Elf with four Moxen; cascade exiles the Harbinger, mana value 2 (a Mountain is first and goes to the bottom of the
# library), and casts it for free; the extra {2} is paid from the three blue mana of a Black Lotus Bot1 sacrifices with the
# cascade trigger on the stack. The Harbinger enters with no tapped creature of an opponent's to return (the trigger has no target).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Bloodbraid Elf
Island
Mountain
Harbinger of the Tides
Island x6

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

